  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Parts are the same as in step 1; nothing added or dropped.",
   "All parts exist in the catalogue; no new part types needed.",
   "The pushbutton is the joystick's integrated select button (SEL on pin 6), so no separate pushbutton is used.",
   "The 10k pulldown is only 'if needed' and the joystick module doesn't need one; the optional left-click button on D3 is omitted.",
   "The optional status LED on pin 5 with a 220 ohm resistor is included as requested, though it isn't in the circuit image. Its placement is my assumption: pin 5 -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED anode, LED cathode -> GND (Leonardo GND.2).",
   "Joystick pins sit in neighbouring columns of one row (11t..15t, row a), one strip per pin, following the catalogue's breadboard facts. The image draws them differently. Each jumper wire goes into row b of the same column as its joystick pin.",
   "Image labels VER/HOR map to catalogue ports VERT/HORZ. Following the image and schematic: A0 goes to VERT and A1 to HORZ."
  ]
 },
